<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Wu of Jin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">236–290</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Sima Yan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a> of Jin, born Sima Yan, was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-jin-dynasty">Western Jin dynasty</a>. In 266 he forced the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a> emperor to abdicate, and in 280 he conquered Eastern Wu, briefly reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>. His enfeoffment of princes with armies prepared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-eight-princes">War of the Eight Princes</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-jin.jpg" alt="Emperor Wu of Jin" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yan Li-pen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jin_Wu_Di.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The failed coup strengthened the Sima clan, and Sima Zhao's son <b>Sima Yan</b> usurped the Wei throne in 266.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-2">2 June in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Wei conquered Shu Han in 263, and in 266 <b>Sima Yan</b> forced Cao Huan to abdicate, founding the Western Jin.</blockquote><a href="/state/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a></li><li><blockquote>After decades in which the Sima family dominated Cao Wei, <b>Sima Yan</b> forced the last Wei emperor to abdicate in 266 and founded the Jin dynasty, ruling from Luoyang as Emperor Wu.</blockquote><a href="/state/western-jin">Western Jin</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=34.66,112.42&amp;year=271" aria-label="Luoyang on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7405 909 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Emperor Wu of Jin"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7855 1179h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7855 1179h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=34.66,112.42&amp;year=271">What was here in 271 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
